# AI context, memory, RAG (I4–I7)

Guides: `docs/ai-platform/04-context-memory-rag.md`, `docs/ai-platform/07-document-extraction.md`.

## I4 — Hash gating

| Surface | Gate |
|---------|------|
| User memory | Content hash before upsert; clear Vertex cache names on change |
| Record narrative | Regenerate only if `narratives[v].sourceHash !== contextHash` |
| Section / template mutations | Invalidate tenant user memory caches |

Do not rewrite docs or burn tokens when content is unchanged.

## I5 — AI docs ≠ business docs

Persist narratives / RAG / insights in **`ai_record_summaries`** (and related AI collections), not as first-class business entity fields. Reserved `aiSummary*` keys are aliases/helpers only.

## I6 — RBAC on live reads

Grounded-chat tools and section assembly filter by the **requesting user’s** permissions / field access. Job/spend read APIs need matching `*.read` / `*.run` permissions.

## I7 — Browser-safe imports

Web may import `@repo/ai-context/storage` only. Covered by web browser-safe import tests.

## Generators

- After UI builder / preset / schema changes: `pnpm generate:ai-context`
- Keep `pnpm check:ai-context` green before merge
- Document extraction: DLP + KMS + review flows in `07-document-extraction.md`

## Vectors

Use `@repo/ai-retrieval` `VectorIndexService` with tenant + access metadata on upsert/search.

## Enforcement

- `pnpm check:ai-context`
- `pnpm --filter @repo/ai-context test`, grounded-chat / summary tests
- `apps/web` browser-safe AI context import test

